  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="41495d20-c4fa-4f99-b895-52a4494b8104" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0"> 
  
  <!--Q#1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="73e4ba8b-5ba4-41b1-8314-aae3db1bcec7" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((-4, 6)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((8, 22)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0, 22)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((-4, 6)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((4, 6)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following points is the vertex of the quadratic function \(f(x)=x^2+8x+22\)?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \((-4, 6)\)</para>
      <para>\((\frac{b}{2})^2=(\frac{8}{2})^2=16\)
        \(f(x)=x^2+8x+16+22-16\)
        \(f(x)=(x+4)^2+6\)
        Vertex: \((-4, 6)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.1.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>


<!--Q2-->
<exercise data-content-id="8585ee96-150f-4228-848f-ad2e0dccfa9c" data-problem-comparator="math" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="f(x)=x^2-2x-8">
  <problem>
    <para>For questions 2 – 4, use the function \(f(x)=(x-4)(x+2)\).</para>

      <para>Write the function in standard form. </para>
    </problem>
  <solution>
    <para>Correct! \(f(x)=x^2-2x-8\)</para>
    <para>Expand:
      \(f(x)=(x-4)(x+2)\)
      \(f(x)=x^2-4x+2x-8\)
      \(f(x)=x^2-2x-8\)</para>
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.2.</para>
  </div>
  </exercise>

<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q3-->
<exercise data-content-id="55fe7e4c-ebc6-43b7-96e9-5c03353479ae" data-problem-comparator="math" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="f(x)=(x-1)^2-9">
  <problem>
    <para>Write the function from question 2 in vertex form. </para>
    </problem>
  <solution>
    <para>Correct! \(f(x)=(x-1)^2-9\)</para>
    <para>Complete the square:
      \(f(x)=x^2 - 2x + 1 - 8 - 1\)
      \(f(x)=(x^2 - 2x + 1) - 9\)
      \(f(x)=(x-1)^2 - 9\)</para>
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.2.</para>
  </div>
  </exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q4-->
<!--Q#4-->
<exercise data-content-id="95479bf9-631e-4a04-ac3e-9a400994015d" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((1, -9)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((1, -9)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((1, 9)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((-1, 9)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((-9, -1)\\)&quot;]">
  <problem>
    <para>Identify the vertex of the quadratic function \(f(x) = (x-1)^2 - 9\).</para>
    </problem>
  <solution>
    <para>Correct! The vertex is \((1, -9)\).</para>
    <para>The function is written in vertex form:
      \(f(x) = (x - h)^2 + k\)
      \(f(x) = (x - 1)^2 - 9\)
      \(h = 1\) and \(k = -9\)
      So, the vertex is \((1, -9)\).
    </para>
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.1.</para>
  </div>
  </exercise>



<!--Interaction End -->



  <!--Q#5-->
<exercise data-content-id="1ed28060-bc51-4003-91db-cfee70fddd12" data-problem-comparator="math" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-1/50">
  <problem>
    <para>For questions 5 - 6, write an equation in vertex form of the quadratic function that has a vertex at \((-4, 1)\) and also goes through the point \((6, -1)\).</para>
      
      <para>Find the value of \(a\) for vertex form in simplest form. </para>
    <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
  </problem>
  <solution>
    <para>Correct! \( \frac{-1}{50} \)</para>
    <para>\(-1=a(6-(-4))^2+1\)
        \(-1=a(10)^2+1\)
        \(-2=100a\)
        \(a=\frac{-2}{100}=\frac{-1}{50}\)</para>
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.3.</para>
  </div>
  </exercise>

<!--Q#6-->
<exercise data-content-id="5cb3fdfc-ced5-4ef0-ae95-b0c6c6541248" data-problem-comparator="math" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="y=\\frac{-1}{50}(x+4)^2+1">
  <problem>
    <para>Write the equation in vertex form. Hint: Be sure to use y = to denote your equation.</para>
    <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
  </problem>
  <solution>
    <para>Correct! \(y=\frac{-1}{50}(x+4)^2+1\)</para>
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.2.</para>
  </div>
  </exercise>

<!--Interaction End -->

  
<!--Q#7-->
<exercise data-content-id="a801a69a-ce71-4fc4-8cf5-402892a8e844" data-problem-comparator="math" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="5/36">
  <problem>
    <para>For questions 7 and 8, write an equation in vertex form of the quadratic function that has a vertex at \((-2, -3)\) and also goes through the point \((4, 2)\).</para>
    <para>Find the value of \(a\) for vertex form in simplest form.</para>
    <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
  </problem>
  <solution>
    <para>Correct! \( \frac{5}{36} \)</para>
    <para>\(2=a(4-(-2))^2+(-3)\)
        \(2=a(6)^2+(-3)\)
        \(2+3=36a+(-3)+3\)
        \(5=36a\)
        \(a=\frac{5}{36}\)</para>
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.3.</para>
  </div>
  </exercise>


<!--Q8-->
<exercise data-content-id="25dd1a17-d959-45a0-9466-755d9d347cff" data-problem-comparator="math" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="y=\frac{5}{36}(x+2)^2-3">
  <problem>
    <para>Write the equation in vertex form. Hint: Be sure to use y = to denote your equation.</para>
    </problem>
  <solution>
    <para>Correct! \(y=\frac{5}{36}(x+2)^2-3\)</para>
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.3.</para>
  </div>
  </exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Q#9-->
<exercise data-content-id="0ea78142-8d2b-4f7c-ad07-60bf616e0e8c" data-problem-comparator="math" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="g(x)=(x+4)^2+6">
  <problem>
    <para>For questions 9 - 10, use the function \(f(x)=x^2\) that is shifted to create the function \(g(x)\) that has a vertex at \((-4, 6)\).</para>
    
    <para>Write \(g(x)\) in vertex form. </para>
    </problem>
  <solution>
    <para>Correct! \(g(x)=(x+4)^2+6\)</para>
    <para>Substitute the vertex in for \((h, k)\):
      \(g(x)=(x-(-4))^2+6\)
      \(g(x)=(x+4)^2+6\)</para>
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.3.</para>
  </div>
  </exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q10-->
<exercise data-content-id="60bd9f86-e40b-4662-9244-1f9ad22d5935" data-problem-comparator="math" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="g(x)=x^2+8x+22">
  <problem>
    <para>Write \(g(x)\) in standard form. </para>
    </problem>
  <solution>
    <para>Correct! \(g(x)=x^2+8x+22\)</para>
    <para>Expand and simplify:
      \(g(x)=(x+4)^2+6\)
      \(g(x)=(x+4)(x+4)+6\)
      \(g(x)=x^2+4x+4x+16+6\)
      \(g(x)=x^2+8x+22\)</para>
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.9.3.</para>
  </div>
  </exercise>
